            "result_text": "Done! I've created `/app/run.py` with the `run_tasks` function. Here's how it works:\n\n- **Concurrency limiting**: Uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to ensure at most `max_concurrent` tasks run simultaneously\n- **Cleanup on interrupt**: When you hit Ctrl+C (KeyboardInterrupt), it cancels all pending tasks and waits for them to finish—allowing any `try/finally` blocks or async context managers in your tasks to run their cleanup code\n- **Re-raises the interrupt**: After cleanup, it re-raises the KeyboardInterrupt so your script can exit cleanly\n\nExample usage:\n```python\nimport asyncio\nfrom run import run_tasks\n\nasync def my_task():\n    try:\n        # Your async work here\n        await asyncio.sleep(10)\n    finally:\n        # This cleanup code runs even on Ctrl+C\n        print(\"Cleaning up!\")\n\nasyncio.run(run_tasks([my_task, my_task, my_task], max_concurrent=2))\n```"
